# Microsoft Enterprise Clean Architecture Structure

## Enterprise Layer Organization

```
src/
├── domain/           # Business logic (no dependencies) - Enterprise domain models
├── application/      # Use cases & services - Enterprise application layer
├── infrastructure/   # External services (API clients) - Enterprise infrastructure
└── presentation/     # Controllers & middleware - Enterprise presentation layer
```

## Enterprise Dependency Rules

- **Domain**: No dependencies on other layers - Pure enterprise business logic
- **Application**: Depends on Domain only - Enterprise use cases
- **Infrastructure**: Implements Domain interfaces - Enterprise external services
- **Presentation**: Depends on Application - Enterprise API layer

## File Naming

- Services: `[name].service.ts`
- Use Cases: `[action].use-case.ts`
- Clients: `[name].client.ts`
- Errors: `[type].errors.ts`

## Key Patterns

- **Strategy**: Video generation ([video-generation.strategy.ts](mdc:src/domain/video/strategies/video-generation.strategy.ts))
- **Factory**: Service creation ([video-generator.factory.ts](mdc:src/domain/video/video-generator.factory.ts))
- **Builder**: Complex objects ([video-options.builder.ts](mdc:src/domain/video/video-options.builder.ts))
- **Use Case**: Business flows ([process-text-message.use-case.ts](mdc:src/application/use-cases/process-text-message.use-case.ts))
- **DI**: TSyringe container ([container.ts](mdc:src/infrastructure/di/container.ts))

## Import Order

1. External dependencies (tsyringe, grammy, etc.)
2. Config imports
3. Domain imports
4. Application imports
5. Infrastructure imports
6. Utilities

Example:

```typescript
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';

import { config } from '../../config/config';
import { STTError } from '../../domain/errors';
import { OpenAIClient } from '../../infrastructure/api/openai/openai.client';
import { logger } from '../../utils/logger';
```
